    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2321" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Amphĭlŏchĭa</span></b> ,
			ae, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀμφιλοχία</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a small province in Acarnania</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic.
				Pis. 40</span></i>; Mann. Gr. 62 sq.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Amphĭlŏchĭ-us</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Amphĭlŏchĭcus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>Amphilochian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Argos Amphilochium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					38, 10</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Argos Amphilochicum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin. 4,
					1, 2, § 5</span></i>
			. —<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Amphĭlŏchi</span></b> ,
			ōrum, m., <i>the
				inhabitants of Amphilochia</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 38,
			3</span></i>.</div>
